01:12:57,000 --> 01:13:03,000
 Then you get this model, which is called the neural autoregressive density estimator, right?

535
01:13:03,000 --> 01:13:11,000
 And this is an old model. So this is a two-layer neural AR model, right?

536
01:13:11,000 --> 01:13:20,000
 And, you know, there are various simplified assumptions that are used instead of using so many different distributions for each position of x.

537
01:13:20,000 --> 01:13:30,000
 What you do is you make this ai and ci parameters independent of i, so you just move the same a and c for all the positions.

538
01:13:30,000 --> 01:13:35,000
 So by doing this, you just reduce the number of parameters, okay?

539
01:13:35,000 --> 01:13:49,000
 Now, I still have a problem, right? And this is that though I have a linear number of parameters, my history is going to get longer and longer with increasing sequence length.

540
01:13:49,000 --> 01:13:58,000
 So how do I get around this problem, right? And this is where transformers come in, okay?

541
01:13:58,000 --> 01:14:09,000
 So what transformers allow us to do using the attention mechanism is to say that look, I know you have the entire history of x1 to xn minus 1,

542
01:14:09,000 --> 01:14:16,000
 but you know what? This entire history is not equally important for the current position n, right?

543
01:14:16,000 --> 01:14:24,000
 And you can learn which parts of the history are more important and which parts of the history are less important, right?

544
01:14:24,000 --> 01:14:35,000
 And this is called the attention base, right? And you know, so and if you have to mask certain positions to make sure that this is auto-aggressive.

545
01:14:35,000 --> 01:14:42,000
 And you know, there are encoder-decoder models using transformers, so part P5, all of these are encoder-decoder models,

546
01:14:42,000 --> 01:14:48,000
 but you could also have decoder-only models, which is what we currently use most of the time.

547
01:14:48,000 --> 01:14:55,000
 In the GPT family, palm, llama, Gemini, all of these are decoder-only models using transformers,

548
01:14:55,000 --> 01:15:02,000
 but this is the basic idea behind auto-aggressive generated models, okay?

549
01:15:02,000 --> 01:15:10,000
 Now, just to give you some idea of how such models are actually used in practice, right?

